      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/claude-tv20-qa-copy-reuse-probe/cat-harness/process/Process_SubKgLifecycle",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns/Process",
      "name": "A sub-KG is staged in place, then leaves for its own repository",
      "summary": "Create a knowledge graph inside a harnessed repository as an instance of its own, grow it there, and when it should leave, stage it for separation and move it whole into a new repository.",
      "description": "Create a knowledge graph inside a harnessed repository as an instance of its own, grow it there, and when it should leave, stage it for separation and move it whole into a new repository. Declared in place with a planned `repository` and a `livesAt` saying where it sits today; staged by one import seam (`<name>/platform.ts`), the separation guard and a self-contained rehearsal; then, each behind an explicit owner confirmation, the repository is created, the staged contents are copied in with their history, the declaration is re-pointed, a fresh clone is verified, and the in-repo copy is frozen in the kept trashcan.\n\nThe light sibling of kg-separation, which splits a graph into a content and a tools repository; this moves a data instance whole, and shares kg-separation's seeding gateway and decision table. DRAWN IN PHASES (owner, 2026-11-08, Q-B1-3 A): it keeps its own grow-in-place and staging steps, and calls the authorise, move and cut-over phases it shares with kg-separation.",
      "enforcement": "strict",
